  "body": "## What changed\n\n`pick::align_from_axes` (#769, both +Y and +X picked) re-composed an identity turn about the part centre onto the held alignment, which left float noise in the origin (e.g. y `-7.499999999999999` vs `-7.5`). `change_of` compares exactly, so re-applying the same picks stored a no-op undo step instead of refusing.\n\nNow a turn below a quarter of the landing tolerance (`LAND_TOL / 4` = 2.5e-10 rad) hands back the held alignment unchanged, and `AlignPartToSetup` refuses \"setup '...' already holds the part that way\". The GUI (Setups page \"Part axes\" Apply, through `check_align` / `align_from_axes`) and MCP `set_part_axes` share that path, so both get the same refusal. The landing proof still runs on the returned alignment. A real turn is built and stored exactly as before; `change_of`, the undo history for real changes and the WCS are untouched.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1347-noop-part-picks.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests. Both failed on the old code (checked by reverting `axis.rs`):\n- `crates/app/tests/align_axes_reapply.rs::re_applying_the_same_two_axis_picks_refuses_as_already_held`: the command and `check_align` refuse by name, nothing is written, and one undo is as modelled.\n- `crates/app/tests/align_axes_reapply.rs::a_real_further_turn_from_the_held_alignment_still_goes_through`: a different pick from the held state is still one undo step, and undo restores the held alignment exactly.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_align_axes.rs::set_part_axes_again_with_the_same_picks_refuses_as_already_held`: MCP refuses by name and adds no undo step.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (app lib, align_axes, align_axes_reapply, axis_align, centre_pick, mcp_align_axes). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests --lib -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI was not launched. The Setups page's Apply greying goes through the same `check_align`, which is pinned headlessly.\n- The one-axis in-plane path (`turn_in_plane`) was not changed. It already snaps to exact quarter turns.\n\nChangelog: Re-applying the same +Y/+X part-axis picks now refuses \"already holds the part that way\" instead of adding a no-op undo step (GUI and MCP `set_part_axes`).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1347\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
